abstract: >-
  A CPU-based C++17 simulator for inelastic minimum-bias proton-proton
  collisions at 14 TeV. It generates events with PYTHIA 8, transports
  particles through a simplified ATLAS/Lorenzetti-like sampling calorimeter
  in Geant4, and writes auditable ROOT output. The software supports fixed and
  Poisson-distributed interactions, deterministic seed provenance,
  multithreaded execution, particle lineage, and detector-cell segmentation.
keywords:
  - "high-energy physics"
  - "minimum bias"
  - "Monte Carlo simulation"
  - "calorimetry"
  - "pile-up"
  - "PYTHIA 8"
  - "Geant4"
  - "ROOT"
